{"name": "bioconductor-pfamanalyzer", "id": "64a7dd3085a67aa7f7907fa8", "package_types": ["conda"], "summary": "Identification of domain isotypes in pfam data", "description": "Protein domains is one of the most import annoation of proteins we have with the Pfam database/tool being (by far) the most used tool. This R package enables the user to read the pfam prediction from both webserver and stand-alone runs into R. We have recently shown most human protein domains exist as multiple distinct variants termed domain isotypes. Different domain isotypes are used in a cell, tissue, and disease-specific manner. Accordingly, we find that domain isotypes, compared to each other, modulate, or abolish the functionality of a protein domain. This R package enables the identification and classification of such domain isotypes from Pfam data.", "home": "https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.17/bioc/html/pfamAnalyzeR.html", "public": true, "access": "public", "owner": {"company": "", "location": "", "login": "bioconda", "name": "bioconda", "url": "", "description": "Bioconda is a distribution of bioinformatics software realized as a channel for the versatile Conda package manager.", "created_at": "2015-09-11 22:59:20.880000+00:00", "user_type": "org"}, "full_name": "bioconda/bioconductor-pfamanalyzer", "url": "http://api.anaconda.org/packages/bioconda/bioconductor-pfamanalyzer", "html_url": "http://anaconda.org/bioconda/bioconductor-pfamanalyzer", "versions": ["1.0.1", "1.2.0", "1.6.0", "1.10.0"], "latest_version": "1.10.0", "platforms": {"noarch": "1.10.0"}, "conda_platforms": ["noarch"], "revision": 10, "license": "MIT", "license_url": null, "dev_url": null, "doc_url": null, "source_git_url": null, "source_git_tag": null, "app_entry": {}, "app_type": {}, "app_summary": {}, "builds": ["r44hdfd78af_0", "r45hdfd78af_0", "r43hdfd78af_0"], "ndownloads": 2177, "releases": [{"version": "1.0.1", "distributions": [], "full_name": "bioconda/bioconductor-pfamanalyzer/1.0.1"}, {"version": "1